matic number of colours, the one whose","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"colour vector (in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" order) is lexicographically least, Khuller and Vazirani’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lexicographically first k-colouring (1991) with k = the component’s χ. So within a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"component colours appear in order of first use, colour classes are numbered by their least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex, a bipartite component is coloured by its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bipartition()"},{"text":" sides (left 0), and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"colorCount == chromaticNumber()"},{"text":". Components are not coupled: a bipartite one keeps two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"colours beside a triangle.","type":"text"}]}}}